{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: sized containers, packages, balls and blocks",
  "description": "About 35 lines (pipeline fixtures mostly) count a container or piece the catalog can't weigh. \
Done: a bundle is a bunch (\"1 bundle scallions\" x5), a USDA portion named by alternatives (\"wedge or slice\") answers to either (\"2 wedge lemon\"), and cited pieces for \"2 stick rhubarb\" (a stalk), \"1 fillet anchovy\" and \"1 package instant ramen noodles\". \
Parser/reader cases: \"1 750-ml bottle dry white wine\" / \"red wine\" (the unit is \"750-ml bottle\", and read_package only knows masses: add metric volumes), \"1 five-pound leg of lamb\" x3 (spelled-out leading weight; bone-in cuts are null aliases anyway), \"1 12- ounce beer\" (a space after the hyphen leaves \"12- ounce beer\" in the item), \"10 -to-12-ounce bag semisweet chocolate chips\" (the parser split a \"10-to-12-ounce\" range), \"1 kabocha squash, roughly 2.5 - 3 pounds\" (weight in the item), \"10 inch flour tortillas\" (an inch size read as the unit), \"1 envelope\" noted \".25 ounce unflavored powdered gelatin\" and \"1 package\" noted \"9 oz. chocolate wafer cookies (such as Nabisco)\" (a parenthetical that leads with a weight and runs on into the item isn't read; \"(.25 oz./3 teaspoons ...)\" is). \
Cited-weight cases: balls (\"1 ball no-knead pizza dough\" x5, \"1 ball pizza dough\", \"1 ball burrata\", \"1 ball fresh mozzarella\"), blocks (\"1/2 block cream cheese\": 8 oz, \"block konnyaku\"), mixes (\"1 envelope taco seasoning\", \"1 envelope brown gravy mix\", \"1 package ranch mix\"), \"1 small can baby corn\", \"1 small jar roasted red peppers\", \"1 jar furikake\" x2, \"2 container petite-creme yogurt\", sized bunches (\"1 large bunch basil\", \"2 large bunch rosemary\", \"3 large stalk rosemary\", \"2-3 bunch dried somen\"), \"6 leaf nappa cabbage\", \"1 small head napa cabbage\", loaves without a sourced loaf weight (\"1 loaf bread\", \"1 loaf unsliced white bread\", \"6 loaf pita bread\" which means pitas), cinnamon/cassia and kombu 2-inch pieces (cinnamon is trace; kombu needs a per-inch weight). SR Legacy and FNDDS (the FDC CSV archives scripts/import-catalog.py downloads) have no piece for most of these; USDA Branded labels would. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora; logs/ingredient-catalog-failures.json once #906 lands) and, once blocked-ingredient-burndown-from-prod lands, the prod report; make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
